  "body": "Fixes #632.\n\nUse the effective request method (resolved options, then Request.method, then GET) for the existing default-retry, payload-serialization, and HEAD-body guards. A prebuilt write Request currently gets a GET-style automatic retry; this contradicts the documented write-safety policy and can replay a write after a retryable response. Its overriding JSON body is also left unserialized.\n\nThe lookup remains lazy so onRequest replacement and method overrides are honored. Numeric retry opt-in, string requests, default options, request headers, transport options and error-message code are unchanged. In particular, this does not include the overlapping FetchError-message work in #583.\n\nAdded 13 cases: all four write methods, GET default retry, explicit POST retry opt-in, explicit and default method overrides, HEAD body guard, JSON body override, onRequest replacement, and two real local-HTTP regressions using the existing test server. Against unchanged production code at 1dbc37fd1ceab832fc7c90cad81b1091c95ba563, 9 fail and 4 pass (28 unrelated tests deselected).\n\nValidation on Windows / Node 22 with the repository-pinned pnpm 10.20.0:\n\n- pnpm test: full lint/format checks and all 41 tests pass, including V8 coverage.\n- pnpm build: passed; bundled distribution and declarations generated.\n- git diff --check: passed.\n\nNo external API calls, dependency changes, or release artifacts are committed. The Node 20/24 and other runtime matrix remain hosted-CI validation; this is a draft. The host's unpinned pnpm initially rejected ignored dependency build scripts, so validation used the packageManager-pinned version rather than changing installation policy or approving scripts.\n",
